{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ee7e39d99b57bc5ae2", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Current Electricity - Test 10", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 40, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923186b"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231868", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d92317ff", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "If a copper wire is stretched to&nbsp;increase its length by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. The percentage increase in resistance of the wire is _____%."}, "options": [{"id": "ad8933", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231800"}, {"id": "550faf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231801"}, {"id": "117e06", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231802"}, {"id": "3ed369", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231803"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231804", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "<p>All resistances in figure are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> each. The value of current &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&#39; is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5e66ee68-f982-4233-9740-f49683194ce6-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 217px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b0b906", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231805"}, {"id": "dcc6f1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231806"}, {"id": "8e156e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231807"}, {"id": "e80b79", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231808"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231809", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a738"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>72</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> long wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> as shown in&nbsp;the figure. The galvanometer jockey is placed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. The&nbsp;galvanometer shows zero deflection.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa7fa89a5-4202-48fb-8d54-fedcec0900ac-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 366px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, to the nearest integer, is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6662b0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923180a"}, {"id": "b4247f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923180b"}, {"id": "85904f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923180c"}, {"id": "725472", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923180d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923180e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f36"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e858a"], "question": {"text": "<p>Two cells are connected in opposition as shown. Cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> emf and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> internal resistance; the cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> emf and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> internal resistance. The terminal potential difference of cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F51b7e0e6-3af8-464c-aa69-c7da2871dedd.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 138px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "584e7b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923180f"}, {"id": "b8be50", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231810"}, {"id": "e6d9ce", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231811"}, {"id": "f8a1c8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231812"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231813", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566d"], "concepts": ["6162fb236ed13040ec84b739"], "question": {"text": "<p>Seawater at a frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>, has permittivity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> and resistivity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. Imagine a parallel plate capacitor is immersed in seawater and is driven by an alternating voltage source <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. Then the conduction current density becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msup></math> times the displacement current density after time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>800</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _______</p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mrow><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4a1808", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231814"}, {"id": "d01b6d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231815"}, {"id": "1ba4ce", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231816"}, {"id": "6fdb64", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231817"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231818", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfab7"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0c"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the given figure, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F437c9d84-5670-4410-bd3a-9ec0f70e4bad-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 181px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "367550", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231819"}, {"id": "a9700e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923181a"}, {"id": "8109c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923181b"}, {"id": "3b5523", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923181c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923181d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "<p>A potential&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is applied across a uniform wire of resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The power dissipation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The wire is then cut into two equal halves and a potential of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is applied across the length of each half. The total power dissipation across two wires is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The ratio of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b36462", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923181e"}, {"id": "f96bab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923181f"}, {"id": "10bef6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231820"}, {"id": "5d2413", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231821"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231822", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4702"], "question": {"text": "Two resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>Ω</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mi>Ω</mi></math> are connected in series with a battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and negligible internal resistance. A voltmeter is used to measure voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>Ω</mi></math> resistance, which gives reading as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The resistance of voltmeter must be _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ω</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "3210dd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231823"}, {"id": "5a2c7d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231824"}, {"id": "b6e9ea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231825"}, {"id": "f54bab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231826"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231827", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb2"], "question": {"text": "Two wires of same length and thickness having specific resistances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively are connected in parallel. The effective resistivity is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;cm</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi></math> to the nearest integer, is ___ ."}, "options": [{"id": "574097", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231828"}, {"id": "49de68", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231829"}, {"id": "67dcf7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923182a"}, {"id": "445903", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923182b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923182c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b19"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the given circuit the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F4f28a9fc-ac4d-4fc3-9c6e-ea2acf32a528-9896822.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 362px; height: 250px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2c668b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923182d"}, {"id": "4b27ed", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923182e"}, {"id": "546e1c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923182f"}, {"id": "471562", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231830"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231831", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566d"], "concepts": ["6162fb236ed13040ec84b739"], "question": {"text": "The current density in a cylindrical wire of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The current through the outer portion of the wire between radial distances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "15ad35", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231832"}, {"id": "5528fd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231833"}, {"id": "bb94d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231834"}, {"id": "65d6f1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231835"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231836", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f36"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e858a"], "question": {"text": "In an electric circuit, a call of certain emf provides a potential difference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> across a load&nbsp;resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;However, it provides a potential difference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> across a load resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>.</mo></math>The emf of the cell is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>.</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "0be9f6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231837"}, {"id": "aad06b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231838"}, {"id": "07d3db", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231839"}, {"id": "b09c16", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923183a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923183b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfab7"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0c"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> wire is bent to form a square loop. A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;supply having an internal resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is connected across one of its sides. The potential drop across the diagonals of the square loop is __________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "bf1a1a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923183c"}, {"id": "b9fd2f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923183d"}, {"id": "36616b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923183e"}, {"id": "758a67", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923183f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231840", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "<p>A resistor dissipates <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>192</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of energy in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> when a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is passed through it. Now, when the current is doubled, the amount of thermal energy dissipated in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is _____________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "980216", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231841"}, {"id": "73caf4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231842"}, {"id": "3b53d9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231843"}, {"id": "870bc7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231844"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231845", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "Two wires $A$ and $B$ are made up of the same material and have the same mass. Wire $A$ has radius of $2.0 \\mathrm{~mm}$ and wire $B$ has radius of $4.0 \\mathrm{~mm}$. The resistance of wire $B$ is $2 \\Omega$. The resistance of wire $A$ is _____$\\Omega$."}, "options": [{"id": "3783f0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231846"}, {"id": "edd338", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231847"}, {"id": "c924e4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231848"}, {"id": "4d5325", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231849"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923184a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "<p>A network of four resistances is connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> battery, as shown in figure. The magnitude of voltage difference between the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is __________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F37c13473-3b6b-4070-b6c7-78164ae09454.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 303px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "db2ec7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923184b"}, {"id": "88ba6b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923184c"}, {"id": "5468ab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923184d"}, {"id": "2ed2b2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923184e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d923184f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2