h/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>; where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "3b7a55", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231855"}, {"id": "83db67", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231856"}, {"id": "ee1608", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231857"}, {"id": "fc842b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231858"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f102ee0e063d9231859", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "A steel rod with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mprescripts/><none/><mo>&#8728;</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and area of cross-section <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is heated from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://ww